    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe acceptance test fetches an owner via `GET /api/owners/{id}` and expects `$.selfLink` to equal `/api/owners/<id>`. `selfLink` is a read-time-derived field on the owner response, so I added it in two places:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains `getSelfLink`/`setSelfLink`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", ...)` plus a `@Named(\"selfLink\")` method returning `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()`, matching the existing derived-field pattern (`displayName`, `salutation`, etc.).\n\nNo new OfficeFloor step was needed \u2014 the existing `RespondWithOwner`/`RespondWithOwnerCreated` already send `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, so the field flows through automatically on both the GET and POST responses.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
